			"SHA": "51d4bddbf442268c76e36e70ef9e176c98fe2c3b"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-01T01:32:25Z",
			"File": [
				"⠇⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				868,
				55
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Rename IPC handler functions to follow PascalCase convention\n\nRename all `handle_*` IPC handler functions in WindServiceHandlers, ConfigurationBridge, TauriIPCServer, and related modules to match the PascalCase naming convention specified in CLAUDE.md. Functions like `handle_commands_execute` → `CommandsExecute`, `handle_configuration_get` → `ConfigurationGet`, `handle_incoming_message` → `IncomingMessage`, etc. The new names align with the command/channel names they service (e.g., `commands:execute` → `CommandsExecute`), improving code clarity and consistency across the Mountain IPC layer.\n\nThis is a pure refactor with no functional changes.",
			"SHA": "9134f4bf64e3333b62d9591a5c58b4764b8d5b47"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-01T01:17:29Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				868,
				2
			],
			"Message": "perf(Mountain): Batch command registration emits to reduce IPC saturation\n\nDuring extension boot, 1000+ `registerCommand` notifications fire in a tight burst (113 extensions × ~10 commands each). Each notification was emitting a separate Tauri event, saturating the shared WKWebView IPC channel that also carries keystroke delivery. Users could type for a split second before the burst hit, then nothing.\n\nAdd a `CommandEmitBatch` struct that buffers commands and flushes after 16ms (one frame), reducing 1000+ individual emits to a single batched `{ commands: [...] }` emit. SkyBridge's listener already accepts both shapes (single `{ id, commandId, kind }` or batch `{ commands: [...] }`), so no Sky changes required.\n\nThis keeps the IPC channel free for keystrokes during extension boot when the renderer is most busy.",
			"SHA": "f304bd408f391d1848c357b909b09e5f5906ae99"
		}
	],
